\subsection{Computational Efficiency}
\label{sec:efficiency}

Token pruning reduces both attention ($\propto L^2$) and feedforward ($\propto L$) costs. For $\pi_{0.5}$ ($N{=}768$ of $L{\approx}900$), $k{=}0.9$ cuts attention FLOPs by ${\sim}$16\% while preserving full SR (98.2\%). For SmolVLA, VTR at $M{=}16$ achieves 87.5\% vision token compression with ${\leq}$1.1\,pp below the passthrough control.

